A||||2||Red2m4||Raced a 'vette||||6||
Z||000000||Red2m4||11-15-2000||09:35 PM||||  This happened in August, but I just thought now to write of it.  I was at a red light when this yellow corvette pulls up next to me. (Early '90s, I think.) They rev the engine a bit.  Now I in a fiero with an auto 4cyl., knew I didn't stand much of a chance.  But, what the heck. So the light turns green and I floor it.  And to my surprise I was ahead!  I could hear the tires squeeling on the vette for at least 3 or 4 seconds.  The car hadn't moved an inch!<BR>I actually saw it in the rearview!  I made it to the next light before they caught up.<BR>The driver (A woman, in case your're wondering.) waved and then turned.  Not exactly a kill to brag about, but it made my day.||||reg||6
Z||000001||KnightRyder31||11-15-2000||10:31 PM||||A kill none the less.||||reg||1
Z||000002||gixxer||11-15-2000||10:37 PM||||I think you've touched on the very reason that mid-engined cars are superior from a performance standpoint; massive traction on the drive wheels. And the harder you accelerate, the more the tires are squeezed onto the road.<BR>The 'Vette guy probably just got thru reading the Road & Track article on mid-engined cars. <BR>I bet you soured his milk!<BR>||||reg||1
